This module gathers and re-exports Scott's Definition 7.1 of the function space. Tokens are pairs of consistent finite sets, the bottom token is the pair of empty sets, a finite set of tokens is consistent when every selection of jointly consistent inputs has jointly consistent outputs, and entailment is the constructive witness form of the least approximable map generated by the token set: some subset has inputs entailed by the given input and output union entailing the given output. It also re-exports the finitary-union algebra, the membership and insertion lemmas for the input and output unions, and the consistency and entailment axioms of the function-space system.
